examples.question_text:
In triangle $ABC$, $AB=7$ cm, $BC=8$ cm and $AC=9$ cm. Find $\angle B$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.142857,3.833259);
\draw (B)--(A)--(C)--cycle;
\path (B)--(A) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.5cm] {angle=A--B--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The opposite side is $AC=9$ cm. The sides meeting at $B$ are $7$ cm and $8$ cm.
$\begin{align*}\cos B&=\dfrac{a^{2}+b^{2}-c^{2}}{2ab}\\\cos B&=\dfrac{7^{2}+8^{2}-9^{2}}{2(7)(8)}\\B&=\cos^{-1}\left(\dfrac{32}{112}\right)\\B&\approx73.40^{\circ}\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.142857,3.833259);
\draw (B)--(A)--(C)--cycle;
\path (B)--(A) node[midway,below] {$a=7\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$b=8\text{ cm}$};
\path (A)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$c=9\text{ cm}$};
\node[below left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.5cm] {angle=A--B--C};
\definecolor{solutionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\node[text=solutionBlue] at (1.1,0.7) {$73.40^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
